        "content": "#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <limits>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    int n = 0;\n    int s = 0;\n    if (std::scanf(\"%d%d\", &n, &s) != 2) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    std::vector<long long> column_totals(static_cast<std::size_t>(n), 0);\n    std::vector<int> rows(static_cast<std::size_t>(s) * static_cast<std::size_t>(n));\n    long long best = std::numeric_limits<long long>::lowest();\n\n    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n        const int slot = row % s;\n        int* stored_row = rows.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(slot) * static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n        const bool replacing = row >= s;\n\n        for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n            int value = 0;\n            std::scanf(\"%d\", &value);\n            if (replacing) {\n                column_totals[static_cast<std::size_t>(col)] +=\n                    static_cast<long long>(value) - stored_row[col];\n            } else {\n                column_totals[static_cast<std::size_t>(col)] += value;\n            }\n            stored_row[col] = value;\n        }\n\n        if (row >= s - 1) {\n            long long window_sum = 0;\n            for (int col = 0; col < s; ++col) {\n                window_sum += column_totals[static_cast<std::size_t>(col)];\n            }\n            if (window_sum > best) {\n                best = window_sum;\n            }\n\n            for (int col = s; col < n; ++col) {\n                window_sum += column_totals[static_cast<std::size_t>(col)] -\n                              column_totals[static_cast<std::size_t>(col - s)];\n                if (window_sum > best) {\n                    best = window_sum;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", best);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Streaming the matrix through a contiguous S-row circular buffer while maintaining per-column totals avoids retaining the full matrix, reducing working-set size when S is small; scanning horizontal windows from the totals preserves O(N²) work with sequential accesses.",
